{{!-- The years a tag spans — "2025 — 2026", or "2026" where it spans one.

	{{> "tag/range" slug=slug}}      called from inside {{#tag}}

	slug   the tag being read

Ghost stores no date range on a tag and Handlebars has no arithmetic, so the two ends are two
queries: the tag's oldest post and its newest. Both are `limit="1"` against an indexed order, and
neither can be replaced by reading the page's own `posts` — the header renders on every page of
the archive, and page 3 carries neither end.

WHY THE SECOND QUERY IS IN A PARTIAL. `filter="tag:{{slug}}"` is resolved against the current
context, and inside a {{#get}} block that context is the query's response — the tag's slug is one
frame up, and the get helper's resolver understands a plain path and a dotted one and nothing
else (`{{../slug}}` fails the render outright with `unsupported path segment ""`). A partial's
hash arguments ARE merged into its context, so handing the slug to tag/range-to.hbs puts it back
within reach of a plain path. --}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tag:{{slug}}" order="published_at asc" limit="1" as |oldest|}}
	{{#if oldest}}
		{{> "tag/range-to" slug=../slug from=oldest.[0].published_at}}
	{{/if}}
{{/get}}
